//? Title: MLP Digit Classification: Nonlinear Hidden Features
//? Subtitle: A hidden layer changes the function class; evaluate it with a fixed split
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Some label patterns cannot be separated by an affine readout of the original inputs. A multilayer
perceptron first learns nonlinear features and then classifies them with softmax. We exhibit XOR's
linear limitation, fit a small hidden-layer model and run a fixed-budget demonstration on bundled
8×8 digits. The original full MNIST workflow and its architecture remain available separately.
)
\toc

> The method

A one-hidden-layer network computes h=ReLU(XW1+b1), z=hW2+b2. Backpropagation chains the softmax
score p-y through W2 and the active ReLU mask. Hidden width H gives DH+H+HK+K parameters.
An explicit XOR construction on x1,x2 in {0,1} is

$$
f(x)=\operatorname{ReLU}(x_1+x_2)-2\operatorname{ReLU}(x_1+x_2-1).
$$
\alttext(Two rectified sums produce zero at both equal-input corners and one at the two unequal-input corners.)

No affine function can assign opposite signs to the two diagonal XOR pairs: adding the two
positive-corner inequalities contradicts adding the negative-corner inequalities. Hidden features
remove that restriction. Training is nonconvex; zero training error says nothing by itself about
held-out performance. The original 784→256→128→10 network has 235146 parameters. This report's
offline dataset model uses 64→32→10, explicit minibatch Adam and fixed pixel scaling by 16; it does not
reproduce that MNIST training budget, split or epsilon-LRP analysis. Use `just run-nn mlp_mnist`
with prepared MNIST files for the original complete workflow.

The concept diagram has a retained TikZ source in `diagrams/mlp_mnist_concept.tikz`.
Regeneration requires LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, and dvisvgm.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/mlp_mnist_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/mlp_mnist_concept.tikz > build/mlp_mnist_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/mlp_mnist_concept.svg build/mlp_mnist_concept.dvi > build/mlp_mnist_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered build/mlp_mnist_concept.svg from local TikZ source.\n'
```
